# Set the dock pose.
#
# POSITION source — at most ONE of use_gps_position / use_pending_antenna /
# preserve_position may be true (any pair is rejected). None set = "use
# docking_pose.position as given" (manual map-drag / settings edit, where the
# operator specifies the location directly).
#
# A dock position that is MEASURED (not typed) always comes from the RAW GPS
# antenna position (/gps/fix projected with the datum), lever-arm-corrected
# ONCE with the yaw this call persists. It never comes from the fused pose or
# from /gps/absolute_pose: while charging, fusion_graph gauge-resets the fused
# pose onto the STORED dock pose and those topics are lever-arm-corrected with
# that pinned yaw, so reading them back on the dock is circular and would just
# re-save the old value.
#
# use_gps_position — capture the position NOW, from the raw antenna samples of
#   the last few seconds. Only meaningful with the robot physically seated on
#   the dock: requires is_charging, RTK accuracy, enough RTK-Fixed samples and
#   a converged fused yaw. Used by the GUI "set dock pose" button.
#
# use_pending_antenna — take the position from the antenna mean that
#   map_server's ~/capture_dock_antenna (std_srvs/Trigger) stored earlier,
#   while the robot WAS on the dock, charging and RTK-Fixed. REQUIRES
#   yaw_source=MOTION. This is the dock calibration's normal write: the dock
#   heading can only be measured by REVERSING OFF the dock, so the antenna is
#   captured first (on the dock) and joined with the yaw afterwards (off the
#   dock) — x, y and yaw are written in ONE call. The is_charging and
#   fused-yaw-convergence gates do NOT apply to this call (they were the
#   capture's job / the fused yaw is neither written nor read); the RTK
#   accuracy gate still does. The pending capture must exist, be younger than
#   map_server's dock_antenna_capture_ttl_s, and is CONSUMED by a successful
#   write.
#
# preserve_position — keep the STORED dock X/Y untouched and write the yaw
#   only. REQUIRES yaw_source=MOTION and a dock position already stored. The
#   calibration's FALLBACK when no capture is pending. Same off-dock situation,
#   same gates as use_pending_antenna. The position is kept on the SERVER side
#   (map_server owns it) rather than echoed back by the caller, so a stale or
#   never-received /map_server_node/docking_pose on the caller can never
#   overwrite it with (0, 0).
#
# yaw_source selects how the ORIENTATION (yaw) is captured, INDEPENDENTLY of
# the position source. Callers MUST set it explicitly; PRESERVE (0) is the
# safe default (never corrupts a good stored yaw):
#   PRESERVE (0) — keep the existing persisted dock_pose_yaw unchanged. Used
#                  for a live on-dock GPS capture: single-antenna GPS gives no
#                  standstill heading and the fused yaw is gauge-pinned to the
#                  existing dock_pose_yaw, so any yaw read back on the dock is
#                  circular (see area_manager.cpp on_set_docking_point notes).
#   REQUEST  (1) — take the yaw from docking_pose.orientation as given. Used
#                  for manual map-drag / settings edit, where the operator is
#                  explicitly setting the heading by hand.
#   MOTION   (2) — take the yaw from the yaw_rad field: a motion-derived,
#                  RTK-gated heading produced by the one-click dock-calibration
#                  action (straight-line reverse under RTK-Fixed). This is the
#                  ONLY non-circular way to correct a stale dock heading.
uint8 PRESERVE=0
uint8 REQUEST=1
uint8 MOTION=2

geometry_msgs/Pose docking_pose
bool use_gps_position
uint8 yaw_source
float64 yaw_rad          # ENU map-frame chassis yaw (rad); used only when yaw_source == MOTION
bool preserve_position   # yaw-only write, keep the stored X/Y (see above); default false
bool use_pending_antenna # x/y from ~/capture_dock_antenna + MOTION yaw (see above); default false
---
bool success
# message: on failure, WHY the request was rejected (which gate, with the
# numbers). On success it is empty — unless the pose was applied in memory but
# could NOT be written to mowgli_robot.yaml, in which case it says so (a caller
# whose point is persistence must treat that as a failure).
string message
# The dock pose now held by map_server (valid when success; unchanged stored
# pose otherwise). Callers report THIS, never their own position estimate.
geometry_msgs/Pose stored_pose
